# 🔄 Riverpod State Management Rules

You are a Riverpod expert for Flutter applications. Follow these CRITICAL state management patterns for the Yanolja clone project.

## 🔴 **MANDATORY PROVIDER PATTERNS**

### **Provider Types Usage** (CRITICAL RULES)

**1. Repository Providers** (Dependency Injection)
```dart
// ✅ REQUIRED: Use Provider for dependency injection
final accommodationRepositoryProvider = Provider<AccommodationRepository>(
  (ref) => AccommodationRepositoryImpl(),
);

// ❌ FORBIDDEN: Direct instantiation in widgets
// Don't: final repository = AccommodationRepositoryImpl();
```

**2. Async Data Providers** (API Calls)
```dart
// ✅ REQUIRED: FutureProvider for async operations
final accommodationListProvider = FutureProvider<List<Accommodation>>((ref) {
  final repository = ref.watch(accommodationRepositoryProvider);
  return repository.getAccommodations();
});

// ✅ REQUIRED: Family providers for parameterized data
final accommodationDetailProvider = FutureProvider.family<Accommodation, String>((ref, id) {
  final repository = ref.watch(accommodationRepositoryProvider);
  return repository.getAccommodationById(id);
});
```

**3. Simple State Providers**
```dart
// ✅ REQUIRED: StateProvider for simple mutable state
final selectedRegionProvider = StateProvider<String?>((ref) => null);
final isLoadingProvider = StateProvider<bool>((ref) => false);

// ❌ FORBIDDEN: Complex objects in StateProvider
// Don't: StateProvider<ComplexObject>
```

## 🎯 **CONSUMER PATTERNS** (MANDATORY)

### **Consumer Widget Usage**
```dart
// ✅ REQUIRED: Consumer for Riverpod state access
Consumer(
  builder: (context, ref, child) {
    final accommodations = ref.watch(accommodationListProvider);
    return accommodations.when(
      loading: () => const CircularProgressIndicator(),
      error: (error, stackTrace) => ErrorWidget(error: error),
      data: (data) => ListView.builder(
        itemCount: data.length,
        itemBuilder: (context, index) => AccommodationListItem(
          accommodation: data[index],
        ),
      ),
    );
  },
)
```

### **ConsumerStatefulWidget Pattern**
```dart
// ✅ REQUIRED: For widgets needing both local and global state
class HotelScreen extends ConsumerStatefulWidget {
  const HotelScreen({super.key});
  
  @override
  ConsumerState<HotelScreen> createState() => _HotelScreenState();
}

class _HotelScreenState extends ConsumerState<HotelScreen> {
  // Local state
  String _selectedRegion = '전체';
  
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    // Global state
    final hotels = ref.watch(hotelListProvider);
    
    return Scaffold(/*...*/);
  }
}
```

## 🚫 **CRITICAL ANTI-PATTERNS**

### ❌ **NEVER DO THESE:**

**1. Provider Access Anti-patterns**
```dart
// ❌ FORBIDDEN: ref.read in build method
Widget build(BuildContext context) {
  final data = ref.read(dataProvider); // WRONG!
  return Text(data.toString());
}

// ✅ CORRECT: ref.watch in build method
Widget build(BuildContext context) {
  final data = ref.watch(dataProvider); // CORRECT!
  return Text(data.toString());
}
```

**2. State Mutation Anti-patterns**
```dart
// ❌ FORBIDDEN: Direct state mutation
ref.read(accommodationListProvider).add(newAccommodation); // WRONG!

// ✅ CORRECT: Use state notifier or refresh
ref.refresh(accommodationListProvider); // CORRECT!
```

**3. Memory Leak Anti-patterns**
```dart
// ❌ FORBIDDEN: Keeping references without disposal
class _MyWidgetState extends ConsumerState<MyWidget> {
  late final StreamSubscription subscription;
  
  @override
  void initState() {
    super.initState();
    // WRONG: No disposal mechanism
    subscription = someStream.listen(/*...*/);
  }
}

// ✅ CORRECT: Proper disposal
class _MyWidgetState extends ConsumerState<MyWidget> {
  @override
  void dispose() {
    subscription.cancel(); // CORRECT!
    super.dispose();
  }
}
```

## ✅ **REQUIRED IMPLEMENTATION PATTERNS**

### **Error Handling Pattern**
```dart
// ✅ REQUIRED: Comprehensive error handling
final dataProvider = FutureProvider<List<Data>>((ref) async {
  try {
    final repository = ref.watch(repositoryProvider);
    return await repository.fetchData();
  } catch (error, stackTrace) {
    // Log error for debugging
    debugPrint('Error fetching data: $error');
    
    // Re-throw for UI handling
    throw Exception('Failed to load data: ${error.toString()}');
  }
});
```

### **Loading State Pattern**
```dart
// ✅ REQUIRED: Proper loading state management
Widget build(BuildContext context) {
  final asyncData = ref.watch(dataProvider);
  
  return asyncData.when(
    loading: () => const Center(
      child: CircularProgressIndicator(),
    ),
    error: (error, stackTrace) => Center(
      child: Column(
        mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.center,
        children: [
          const Icon(Icons.error_outline, size: 48),
          const SizedBox(height: 16),
          Text('Error: ${error.toString()}'),
          ElevatedButton(
            onPressed: () => ref.refresh(dataProvider),
            child: const Text('Retry'),
          ),
        ],
      ),
    ),
    data: (data) => ListView.builder(
      itemCount: data.length,
      itemBuilder: (context, index) => ListTile(
        title: Text(data[index].name),
      ),
    ),
  );
}
```

### **Refresh Pattern**
```dart
// ✅ REQUIRED: RefreshIndicator with provider refresh
RefreshIndicator(
  onRefresh: () async {
    // Refresh the provider
    ref.refresh(accommodationListProvider);
    
    // Wait for the refresh to complete
    return ref.read(accommodationListProvider.future);
  },
  child: ListView(/*...*/),
)
```

## 📋 **PROVIDER ORGANIZATION**

### **File Structure** (MANDATORY)
```
lib/presentation/provider/
├── accommodation_provider.dart      # Accommodation-related providers
├── auth_provider.dart              # Authentication providers  
├── booking_provider.dart           # Booking-related providers
├── saved_provider.dart             # Saved items providers
└── search_provider.dart            # Search-related providers
```

### **Provider Naming Convention**
```dart
// ✅ REQUIRED: Descriptive names with Provider suffix
final accommodationListProvider = FutureProvider<List<Accommodation>>(/*...*/);
final accommodationDetailProvider = FutureProvider.family<Accommodation, String>(/*...*/);
final selectedHotelRegionProvider = StateProvider<String?>(/*...*/);

// ❌ FORBIDDEN: Generic or unclear names
// final dataProvider = FutureProvider(/*...*/); // WRONG!
// final listProvider = FutureProvider(/*...*/); // WRONG!
```

## 🔍 **TESTING REQUIREMENTS**

### **Provider Testing Pattern**
```dart
// ✅ REQUIRED: Test providers with ProviderContainer
void main() {
  test('accommodationListProvider should return accommodations', () async {
    final container = ProviderContainer(
      overrides: [
        accommodationRepositoryProvider.overrideWithValue(
          MockAccommodationRepository(),
        ),
      ],
    );
    
    final result = await container.read(accommodationListProvider.future);
    expect(result, isA<List<Accommodation>>());
    
    container.dispose();
  });
}
```

## 🎯 **PERFORMANCE CHECKLIST**

Before implementing providers, ensure:
- [ ] Using appropriate provider type (Provider vs StateProvider vs FutureProvider)
- [ ] Family providers for parameterized data
- [ ] Proper error handling in all async providers  
- [ ] ref.watch in build methods, ref.read in event handlers
- [ ] Provider disposal for complex state notifiers
- [ ] No provider access in initState (use ref.listen instead)
- [ ] Refresh mechanism implemented for data providers
- [ ] Loading states handled in UI

## 🚨 **CRITICAL WARNINGS**

**NEVER:**
- Use ref.read inside build methods
- Create providers inside widgets
- Mutate provider state directly
- Forget to handle loading/error states
- Access providers before widget mounting
- Create circular dependencies between providers